BitChord-specific adaptations
-----------------------------
The backdrop engine under ui/components/backdrop/ is kept byte-identical to
Convx's apart from its package name, so it can be re-synced by re-copying
Convx's ui/component/backdrop/ and rewriting
`com.convx.music.ui.component.backdrop` -> `com.music.bitchord.ui.components.backdrop`.

The handful of places where BitChord has to supply app-level context that
Convx keeps outside the engine are in
ui/components/backdrop/ConvxBackdropCompat.kt:

  - LocalAmbientBackgroundColor, LocalAmbientDarkChrome, LocalSampledChromeDark
      Convx declares these at its root; they hold MutableState and default to
      Color.Unspecified / null. BitChord has no sampled-chrome pipeline, so
      LocalSampledChromeDark stays null and the engine falls back to the
      ambient path, exactly as Convx does when no sample is available.

  - lastNavWasPop()
      Convx's "a nav transition is popping" flag, read by
      backdrops/NavTransitionFreeze.kt. BitChord's shells do not currently
      drive it, so it stays false and layers sample live.

  - markNavTransitionIsPop(Boolean)
      BitChord-side setter for the flag above, for when a shell does drive it.

In GlassEffect.kt, Convx's AppTheme.colorScheme.surface.luminance() is read
through BitChord's MaterialTheme surface role, which is the same final
fallback in Convx's own appearance decision.

