SpotiFLAC Mobile — MIT License
================================================================================
Source:  https://github.com/spotiflacapp/SpotiFLAC-Mobile
License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 zarzet)

BitChord copies no SpotiFLAC code — the app is Flutter and this one is Kotlin.
What is derived from studying it: the shader-warmup technique (their
MornyeGlassWarmup rasterises the glass pipeline once before any frame needs
it; GlassShaderWarmup does the equivalent for this app's AGSL shaders at
startup) and the interaction-gating trade (their liquid lens takes
`interaction: false` for the duration of a gesture; this app freezes its
backdrop during the Now Playing sheet's motion for the same reason). Their
liquid_glass_easy parameter mapping (clarity -> vibrancy, blurSigma ->
blurRadius, refraction -> lens, dispersion -> chromaticAberration,
highlightIntensity -> highlightOpacity) informed the Liquid Glass intensity
setting's scaling.

